       title="JirAI" id="JirAI">


    <link-summary>Documentation for JirAI, the Jira Cloud plugin for JetBrains IDEs.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Browse, create, edit and plan Jira Cloud work from your JetBrains IDE.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>JirAI brings Jira Cloud into JetBrains IDEs: browse and edit issues, run Kanban and Scrum boards, push Markdown docs and give AI assistants Jira context.</web-summary>

    <section-starting-page>
        <title>JirAI</title>
        <description>
            Work with Jira Cloud issues, boards and space reports without leaving your JetBrains IDE.
            JirAI also turns Markdown specs into Jira issues and lets AI assistants check a draft against your project's real create screen.
            JirAI is a paid plugin with a 7-day free trial.
        </description>

        <spotlight>
            <a href="JirAI-Installation.topic" type="start" summary="Install the plugin, start the 7-day trial and check the requirements.">Install JirAI</a>
            <a href="Work-with-Jira-Issues.topic" type="tools" summary="Search, filter and open Jira Cloud issues in the JirAI tool window.">Work with issues</a>
        </spotlight>

        <primary>
            <title>Work with Jira</title>
            <a href="JirAI-Sign-In-and-Configuration.topic" type="start" summary="Sign in to your Jira Cloud site with an Atlassian API token and manage the account.">Sign in</a>
            <a href="Jira-Create-Issues.topic" type="tools" summary="Create issues from your project's own create screen, with Markdown descriptions.">Create issues</a>
            <a href="Jira-Issue-Details-and-Editing.topic" type="mixed" summary="Edit fields in place, move issues through the workflow and manage attachments.">Issue details</a>
            <a href="Jira-Timeline-and-Description-Editor.topic" type="development" summary="Read the activity feed, comment, edit the description and see child work items.">Timeline and breakdown</a>
            <a href="JirAI-Board.topic" type="integration" summary="Open a Kanban board or a Scrum sprint and move cards between columns.">Board</a>
            <a href="JirAI-Metrics.topic" type="cloud" summary="Summary charts, a hierarchical list and flow reports for any Jira space.">Spaces</a>
            <a href="JirAI-AI-Workflows.topic" type="development" summary="Create or update a Jira issue from a Markdown spec or plan.">Push Markdown docs</a>
            <a href="JirAI-Agent-Tools.topic" type="integration" summary="Let an AI assistant read the create screen and check drafts against your house standard.">Agent tools</a>
        </primary>

        <secondary>
            <title>Set up and get help</title>
            <a href="JirAI-Whats-New.topic" type="learn" summary="Changes in recent JirAI releases, newest first.">What's new</a>
            <a href="JirAI-Settings-Reference.topic" type="settings" summary="Every JirAI settings page and option in one place.">Settings reference</a>
            <a href="JirAI-FAQ.topic" type="support" summary="Answers to common questions and the known limitations.">FAQ</a>
            <a href="JirAI-Reference-and-Support.topic" type="support" summary="Report a problem, contact the vendor and read the legal terms.">Support</a>
